cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: groundfault
abstract: >-
  groundfault evaluates staged earth-fault tests in compensated (resonant-earthed) medium-voltage networks from
  COMTRADE recordings: the residual earth-fault current and its harmonics, voltages and assessment quantities with
  measurement uncertainty; the residual current at any earthing impedance from a series of tests with different fault
  impedances (equivalent-source method); the earth potential rise and touch voltage at secondary substations per
  frequency, as measured and fault-related by superposition, the current into the LV network and the earthing
  impedance of the LV network; the reduction factor compared with earthing measurements stored in a groundmeas
  database; and the forecast of the harmonic residual current from harmonic voltages – without an earth fault from
  network data and undisturbed recordings of the transformer node, and with a network model of the busbar per
  harmonic order, calibrated with staged tests and updated with recorded earth faults. Jupyter notebooks serve as the
  user interface; output is available in English and German.
authors:
